      "writtenOn": "2018-01-15T00:00:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the idea to have one SignerConfig for each old signing key/cert? If so, this setter approach doesn\u0027t support more than one old signing key.\n\nWould having a single SingerConfig contain the latest + older signing keys work?",
      "revId": "be3b87f143fe6382aa8f63fb04f274d9af2e706e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4556740_19967200",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/android/apksig/ApkSigner.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1026058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-16T19:03:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is the idea, but v3 signature scheme explicitly decided not to support multiple-signer situations, so this method should only ever need to be set with one signer.\n\nThis could be done by adding an older signer to every new signer, but given the above design decision, I\u0027m not sure what it buys us.  I tried a few different combinations of this, and keeping the singers separate allowed me to change less code, I think, in the end.",
      "parentUuid": "e7a5c736_9b8e59d5",
      "revId": "be3b87f143fe6382aa8f63fb04f274d9af2e706e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88cb5911_b636c009",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/android/apksig/ApkSigner.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1018773
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-16T21:23:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I meant is that there will be situations where you need to provide more than 2 keys for a single signer. For example, let\u0027s say I rotate signing key from RSA to EC. I now need to provide 2 keys to sign the APK: the RSA and EC key. I then rotate the signing key to to an EdDSA one, supported only one some newer platforms. Now I need to provide 3 keys to sign the APK. However, the approach in this code doesn\u0027t appear to let me provide more than two keys.",
      "parentUuid": "b4556740_19967200",
      "revId": "be3b87f143fe6382aa8f63fb04f274d9af2e706e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61f09030_fdaca792",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/android/apksig/ApkSigner.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1026058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-16T21:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) rotate from RSA to EC\n- you would need to sign with RSA key for v1 and v2 (setOldSignerConfig), and sign with EC key in the normal signer configs, with minSdkVersion 0 and maxSdkVersion INT_MAX, you would also need to provide a SigningCertificateLineage which says v1 -\u003e v2 is ok\n2) rotating to EdDSA key, for plat version 30+\n- you would still need to provide RSA key for v1 and v2 signing (setOldSignerConfig), you would then provide two signers as part of the normal SignerConfigs:\n    * the same one provided in step 1, except minSdkVersion is now 0 and max is 29\n    * a new one with minSdkVersion 30, which also includes the SigningCertificateLineage for RSA-\u003eEC-\u003eEdDSA.  In both cases, only one oldSignerConfig is needed (and it\u0027s the same for both new signers).  The other two keys are provided via the normal mechanism for multiple signers, with the restriction that both of those need to have proper SigningCertificateLineage chains, and that they can\u0027t have overlapping sdkVersions.",
      "parentUuid": "88cb5911_b636c009",
      "revId": "be3b87f143fe6382aa8f63fb04f274d9af2e706e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5e1bc02_e04b0759",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/android/apksig/ApkSigner.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1018773
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-17T01:36:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. It would be great if all this complexity, including figuring out whether there is one or more signers, were hidden from the client of this library. Ideally, the client should only need to provide 1 x key lineage, and 3 x private keys. No min-maxSdkVersions, no multiple signers. Given that we had a concept of multiple signers exposed to clients already, ideally the client would still see this situation as a single signer, just with three keys + apksig doing some magic.\n\nIt\u0027s your call though. Perhaps there is a need to expose more controls for clients of apksig and exposing those additional controls breaks this idillic simple solution.",
      "parentUuid": "61f09030_fdaca792",
      "revId": "be3b87f143fe6382aa8f63fb04f274d9af2e706e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7d33249_04c7aebb",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/android/apksig/ApkSigner.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1026058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-17T18:07:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that would be better, but I was wary of design paralysis and my general approach is to do the simple thing first and improve upon it as necessary.  In the vast majority of actual use cases, clients won\u0027t need to change at all (no rotation) and even with rotation, will act the same.\n\nThat being said, it might be more prudent to assume we get this information from the key lineage and make sure we don\u0027t expose any API that we would have to support later.  I\u0027ll consider the implications and changes required of \"one key lineage to rule them all\" as we had discussed previously, but likely will leave the current patch series as-is (unmerged) for purpose of generating CTS and platform changes for key rotation to be able to test the platform.",
      "parentUuid": "a5e1bc02_e04b0759",
      "revId": "be3b87f143fe6382aa8f63fb04f274d9af2e706e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
